OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786403882
OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,FThe number of people on zero-hours
OL,7,Fcontracts in the UK has risen to a
OL,8,Frecord high, despite plans to
OL,9,Fcrackdown on their use, according to a
OL,10,Freport shared exclusively with ITV
OL,11,FNews.
OL,13,FThere are currently 1.24 million
OL,14,Fpeople employed on zero-hours
OL,15,Farrangements, up by 207,000 since
OL,16,FLabour took power in July 2024 with a
OL,17,Fpledge to ban "exploitative" contracts.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G1/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31402
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786403882
OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,FUnder a zero-hours contract, workers
OL,7,Fhave no guarantee of any shifts and
OL,8,Fare only called upon when they're
OL,9,Fneeded - often with very little notice
OL,10,F- meaning many have no idea how much
OL,11,Fthey will earn from month to month.
OL,13,FShifts can be cancelled at the last
OL,14,Fminute and workers are not entitled to
OL,15,Fany compensation, despite often
OL,16,Falready paying for transport and
OL,17,Fchildcare.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31403
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786403882
OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,FLabour had initially pledged - before
OL,7,Ftheir 2024 manifesto - to protect
OL,8,Fworkers by banning zero-hours
OL,9,Fcontracts entirely, before watering
OL,10,Fthis down to only outlaw
OL,11,F"exploitative" zero-hours contracts.
OL,13,FBusinesses, and some workers, say zero-
OL,14,Fhours contracts are beneficial because
OL,15,Fthey allow flexibility, and the
OL,16,Fhospitality industry has warned that a
OL,17,Fcrackdown could devastate the sector.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31404
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786403882
OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,FHowever, research carried out by the
OL,7,FLancaster University's Work
OL,8,FFoundation, on behalf of the Trades
OL,9,FUnion Congress (TUC), found a record
OL,10,Fnumber of zero-hours contract workers
OL,11,Fdepend on their contract for full-time
OL,12,Fwork (32.8%).
OL,14,FThe research found 77% are not in full-
OL,15,Ftime education, suggesting a large
OL,16,Fproportion of workers don't need that
OL,17,Fflexibility.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31405
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786403882
OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,FAs part of the research, the Work
OL,7,FFoundation followed nine zero-hours
OL,8,Fworkers for a week, to learn about
OL,9,Flife on those contracts. The research
OL,10,Ffound:
OL,12,FThe Work Foundation at Lancaster
OL,13,FUniversity said the flexibility of
OL,14,Fzero-hours contracts is one sided in
OL,15,Ffavour of the business, leaving
OL,16,Fworkers "highly vulnerable to late
OL,17,Fchanges and cancellations of their
OL,18,Fshifts".
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31406
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786403882
OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,FBen Harrison, director of the Work
OL,7,FFoundation added: "This can make it
OL,8,Fextremely difficult to plan for day-to-
OL,9,Fday expenses like childcare, and for
OL,10,Flong-term financial commitments like
OL,11,Frenting or buying a home.
OL,13,F"Government must now deliver on its
OL,14,Fcommitment to end exploitative zero-
OL,15,Fhour contracts by giving workers at
OL,16,Fleast 28 days' notice of shifts,
OL,17,Fensuring full pay for late
OL,18,Fcancellations, and putting strong
OL,19,Fenforcement behind the new reforms."
OL,26,@uD@AOU{D@dO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/17
