OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,FThe plan under Keir Starmer's
OL,7,Fgovernment, which his successor Andy
OL,8,FBurnham could change following
OL,9,Fconsultation, would force firms to
OL,10,Foffer a minimum number of hours each
OL,11,Fweek based on their regular working
OL,12,Fhours over a 12-week reference period.
OL,14,FMinisters said they wanted workers to
OL,15,Fbe guaranteed a minimum of between
OL,16,Feight and 20 hours a week if their
OL,17,Fcurrent contracts were at or below
OL,18,Fthat level.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31409
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786403882
OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,FWorkers would be able to choose a zero-
OL,7,Fhours contract if they preferred, but
OL,8,Fthey would be eligible for
OL,9,Fcompensation if their shifts are
OL,10,Fchanged at short notice.
OL,12,FMinisters said the reforms will help
OL,13,Fsave workers in some of the most
OL,14,Fdeprived areas up to #600 in lost
OL,15,Fincome from the hidden costs of
OL,16,Finsecure work.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31410
SC,0010
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786403882
OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,FHowever, the hospitality industry says
OL,7,Fbeing forced to pay compensation would
OL,8,Fbe crippling financially, and they
OL,9,Fwant the 12-week reference period
OL,10,Fdoubled to 24 weeks, so they don't
OL,11,Fhave to guarantee hours long-term to
OL,12,Fseasonal workers.
OL,14,FRetail and hospitality bosses, who
OL,15,Foften hire younger people, say the
OL,16,Freforms could drive up the number of
OL,17,F16 to 24 year olds who are not in
OL,18,Femployment or education, which stands
OL,19,Fat over a million.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G10/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31411
SC,0011
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786403882
OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,FAllen Simpson, chief executive of
OL,7,Ftrade body UK Hospitality, said: "Jobs
OL,8,Fin hospitality are critical for
OL,9,Fsupporting people who need flexible
OL,10,Fhours and jobs, from working parents
OL,11,Fto those with caring responsibilities.
OL,13,FHe added: "There is a danger that over-
OL,14,Fregulating flexible work actually
OL,15,Fincreases work instability, rather
OL,16,Fthan decrease it, which would
OL,17,Fundermine the government's agenda to
OL,18,Fget people back into work. That must
OL,19,Fbe avoided at all costs."
OL,26,@oD@bOUuD@KOU{D@YO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G11/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31412
SC,0012
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786403882
OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,FHelen Dickinson, chief executive of
OL,7,Fthe British Retail Consortium (BRC),
OL,8,Fsaid: "It's vital that we don't
OL,9,Fregulate flexible jobs out of
OL,10,Fexistence.
OL,12,F"Flexible and part-time work is how
OL,13,Fmillions of people make employment
OL,14,Fwork for them ` balancing shifts
OL,15,Falongside study, childcare or caring
OL,16,Fresponsibilities, and retail plays a
OL,17,Fvital role in providing those
OL,18,Fopportunities.
OL,26,@pD@GOUtD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G12/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31413
SC,0013
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786403882
OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,F"For many workers, that flexibility
OL,7,Fisn't (just) nice to have ` it's what
OL,8,Fmakes employment possible and allows
OL,9,Fthem to take on extra hours when it
OL,10,Fsuits them.
OL,12,F"Retailers need to offer those
OL,13,Fadditional hours when demand is there,
OL,14,Fbut they cannot guarantee them all-
OL,15,Fyear round."
OL,17,FThe TUC denies action on zero-hours
OL,18,Fcontracts would drive up unemployment,
OL,19,Flabelling warnings as "bad faith
OL,20,Fscaremongering".
OL,26,@nD@AOUtD@AOUwD@LO]{D@WOU|D@OO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G13/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31414
SC,0014
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786403882
OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,FThe organisation, which represents
OL,7,Fdozens of unions including 5.3 million
OL,8,Fworkers, says that "zero-hours
OL,9,Fcontracts are a dream for bad bosses
OL,10,Fand a nightmare for workers".
OL,12,FUrging Burnham to stick with his
OL,13,Fpredecessor's plans, TUC General
OL,14,FSecretary Paul Nowak said: "This
OL,15,Fresearch shows just how difficult it
OL,16,Fis to get by, and to plan your life,
OL,17,Fon these exploitative contracts.
OL,26,@vD@\OU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G14/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31415
SC,0015
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786403882
OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,F"The contracts also make it harder to
OL,7,Fraise issues with your boss due to
OL,8,Fpower imbalances. And not just that `
OL,9,Fthey encourage poor management
OL,10,Fpractices which are bad for workers
OL,11,Fand bad for the wider economy.
OL,13,F"That's why the new prime minister
OL,14,Fmust take on the broken status quo and
OL,15,Fput an end to exploitative zero hours
OL,16,Fcontracts by delivering these new
OL,17,Frights to guaranteed hours at pace and
OL,18,Fin full."
OL,26,@nD@AOUuD@AOUzD@IO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G15/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31416
SC,0016
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786403882
OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,FInsisting that it would be going ahead
OL,7,Fwith the reforms, a spokesperson for
OL,8,FBurnham's government said: "We are
OL,9,Fabsolutely committed to ending
OL,10,Fexploitative zero hours contracts.
OL,12,F"These reforms will give workers in
OL,13,Fevery postcode greater income security
OL,14,Fand predictability of hours. We have
OL,15,Fengaged extensively with trade unions
OL,16,Fand the TUC on our measures.
OL,18,F"We know zero hours contracts can work
OL,19,Ffor some people, workers will be able
OL,20,Fto decline a guaranteed hours contract
OL,21,Fif they want to.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G16/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31417
SC,0017
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786403882
OL,3,CRecord number relying on zero-hours
OL,4,Ccontracts despite crackdown plans
OL,6,F"We're consulting on the proposals and
OL,7,Fgiving businesses and workers a chance
OL,8,Fto have their say."
OL,10,FFrom Westminster to Washington DC -
OL,11,Four political experts are across all
OL,12,Fthe latest key talking points. Listen
OL,13,Fto the latest episode below...
